535
00:31:17,609 --> 00:31:19,076
Yo, taxi!

536
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:39,889
Wait for me.

537
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:42,158
I'll be right at the
block, Mr. Kramer.

538
00:33:22,700 --> 00:33:25,535
I almost got my hand
on it, almost got it.

539
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:28,237
Hey.

540
00:33:28,306 --> 00:33:30,540
Now, that's what I
call real power dining.

541
00:33:30,609 --> 00:33:32,742
Thomas Baldwin
and Edward Kramer,

542
00:33:32,810 --> 00:33:34,655
but I don't recognize
the gentleman on the left.

543
00:33:34,679 --> 00:33:35,878
Do you know his name?

544
00:33:35,947 --> 00:33:37,680
Mr. Kramer, company.

545
00:33:37,749 --> 00:33:39,015
Get him.

546
00:34:07,813 --> 00:34:11,114
♪ ♪

547
00:34:42,714 --> 00:34:45,715
♪ ♪

548
00:35:07,372 --> 00:35:10,307
♪ ♪

549
00:35:36,701 --> 00:35:37,701
Alex. Oh!

550
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:40,069
Sorry.

551
00:35:40,138 --> 00:35:41,249
You all right? Yeah.

552
00:35:41,273 --> 00:35:43,539
Uh, yeah, the coffee
shop's open all night,

553
00:35:43,608 --> 00:35:46,042
and they, they sell this stuff
that settles your stomach.

554
00:35:46,111 --> 00:35:48,111
How's the stakeout?

555
00:35:48,180 --> 00:35:49,445
Shelby Russell's in 1402.

556
00:35:49,514 --> 00:35:50,658
All right, let's go.

557
00:35:50,682 --> 00:35:52,727
Well, you missed a
busy night last night.

558
00:35:52,751 --> 00:35:54,116
Yeah, what happened?

559
00:35:54,185 --> 00:35:56,731
A couple of your average hoods
tried to make a move on me.

560
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:58,800
Had to throw a little
karate on 'em, you know,

561
00:35:58,824 --> 00:36:01,791
a little flying crane, a
little spinning dervish.

562
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:04,661
I mean, both hands, both
feet going at the same time.

563
00:36:04,730 --> 00:36:05,930
Yeah?

564
00:36:06,832 --> 00:36:08,597
It knocked 'em out, man.

565
00:36:13,772 --> 00:36:15,483
So, we just have
to find out the name

566
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:17,017
of the third guy at the table.

567
00:36:17,041 --> 00:36:19,175
No, we already
know the third guy.

568
00:36:19,243 --> 00:36:20,943
That was Dr. Douglas Clark.

569
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:22,779
He had MD plates on his car.

570
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:23,913
I had him checked out.

571
00:36:23,981 --> 00:36:25,192
All right, so...

572
00:36:25,216 --> 00:36:27,261
Thomas Baldwin, Edward Kramer

573
00:36:27,285 --> 00:36:29,397
and Dr. Douglas Clark
are Misters A, B and C.

574
00:36:29,421 --> 00:36:31,399
Right... it's Kramer
that interests me.

575
00:36:31,423 --> 00:36:32,900
He's into big-time crime.

576
00:36:32,924 --> 00:36:34,001
Right.

577
00:36:34,025 --> 00:36:36,158
Oh, I spoke to Mr. Reese today.

578
00:36:36,227 --> 00:36:37,405
What did he want?

579
00:36:37,429 --> 00:36:39,206
Well, he wanted to
express the strong opinion

580
00:36:39,230 --> 00:36:40,508
of Benson, Reese,
Kline & Dunhill

581
00:36:40,532 --> 00:36:42,264
that Anthony Stewart
return to London.

582
00:36:42,334 --> 00:36:44,266
But I told him that
we had the case

583
00:36:44,336 --> 00:36:45,680
completely under control.

584
00:36:53,278 --> 00:36:55,545
Mrs. Russell?

585
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:08,291
She's gone, Alex.

586
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:10,092
She's gone?

587
00:37:17,302 --> 00:37:19,235
Couldn't be gone long.

588
00:37:34,319 --> 00:37:37,120
♪ ♪

589
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:48,443
This is a high-price town.

590
00:37:48,467 --> 00:37:49,499
So?

591
00:37:49,568 --> 00:37:50,778
Well, she couldn't
have gone far.

592
00:37:50,802 --> 00:37:52,080
She left here on foot.

593
00:37:52,104 --> 00:37:53,247
You take uptown.

594
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:54,551
I'll go downtown.

595
00:37:54,606 --> 00:37:55,838
All right, great, okay.

596
00:38:04,182 --> 00:38:06,682
<i>Okay...</i> how much I owe you?

597
00:38:06,752 --> 00:38:08,151
$11.50.

598
00:38:08,219 --> 00:38:11,253
$11.50... There's 12 bucks.

599
00:38:11,322 --> 00:38:13,923
Keep the change.

600
00:38:13,991 --> 00:38:16,025
Keep the change?

601
00:38:19,164 --> 00:38:21,064
Keep the change.

602
00:38:21,132 --> 00:38:23,999
See what it's like
to keep<i> my</i> change.

603
00:38:28,373 --> 00:38:30,151
Hey! Hey, Plaid Coat!

604
00:38:30,175 --> 00:38:32,108
Hey, Plaid Coat!

605
00:38:32,176 --> 00:38:33,442
Give me my wallet back!

606
00:38:33,511 --> 00:38:36,112
Hey, my wallet!

607
00:38:39,184 --> 00:38:41,083
Jackass.

608
00:39:13,051 --> 00:39:15,684
Uh... Mr. Kramer?

609
00:39:17,155 --> 00:39:19,466
Uh, my name is Ben Matlock.

610
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:23,292
Uh, I'm, uh, Anthony
Stewart's attorney.

611
00:39:23,362 --> 00:39:25,261
Oh, yeah.

612
00:39:25,330 --> 00:39:27,408
Yeah, I saw your name
in the paper last night.

613
00:39:27,432 --> 00:39:29,477
I wonder if I could ask
you a few questions

614
00:39:29,501 --> 00:39:30,834
about Michael Russell.

615
00:39:30,902 --> 00:39:32,401
I understand you knew him.

616
00:39:32,471 --> 00:39:34,637
Show Mr. Matlock
where he can change.

617
00:39:34,706 --> 00:39:35,905
You'll have a massage.

618
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:36,974
Relax.

619
00:39:37,008 --> 00:39:38,048
Oh, no... no, thanks.

620
00:39:38,109 --> 00:39:39,041
No, thanks.

621
00:39:39,110 --> 00:39:40,376
Sit, Mr. Matlock.

622
00:39:40,445 --> 00:39:42,078
Take off your coat.

623
00:39:44,749 --> 00:39:46,048
Okay.

624
00:39:46,117 --> 00:39:47,383
Now, what makes you think

625
00:39:47,452 --> 00:39:48,985
I knew the man your client

626
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:51,387
is supposed to have
murdered, Mr. Matlock?

627
00:39:51,456 --> 00:39:53,234
Well, we have this
ledger we found

628
00:39:53,258 --> 00:39:54,435
in Michael Russell's office,

629
00:39:54,459 --> 00:39:56,637
and apparently, it had to do

630
00:39:56,661 --> 00:39:59,862
with the pharmaceutical
company that he owned,

631
00:39:59,931 --> 00:40:02,932
and it looks like that he
had three secret partners

632
00:40:03,001 --> 00:40:06,502
listed only as A, B
and C, and... and I...

633
00:40:06,571 --> 00:40:09,705
I just wondered...

634
00:40:09,774 --> 00:40:12,575
Now, there are thousands
of people in this city

635
00:40:12,644 --> 00:40:14,744
who could be A, B or C.

636
00:40:14,812 --> 00:40:17,980
Well, you had a meeting
with Thomas Baldwin

637
00:40:18,049 --> 00:40:19,827
and Douglas Clark last night.

638
00:40:19,851 --> 00:40:22,151
They could certainly be B and C.

639
00:40:23,422 --> 00:40:25,254
What's your point?

640
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:28,858
Could you be A?

641
00:40:33,231 --> 00:40:35,498
This is New York, Mr. Matlock.

642
00:40:35,567 --> 00:40:37,300
One meets many diverse people.

643
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:39,903
We're friends, nothing more.

644
00:40:39,971 --> 00:40:41,938
Uh-huh.

645
00:40:42,007 --> 00:40:46,209
Well... uh... uh, this
was certainly very nice.

646
00:40:46,278 --> 00:40:47,343
Thank you.

647
00:40:47,412 --> 00:40:49,379
Are you sure you
wouldn't like to change?

648
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:51,114
Have a full body massage?

649
00:40:51,182 --> 00:40:52,248
Oh, no, thanks.

650
00:40:52,317 --> 00:40:54,650
What he did to my
neck fixed me right up.

651
00:41:27,252 --> 00:41:30,186
♪ ♪

652
00:41:49,207 --> 00:41:51,941
No initials, nothing.

653
00:41:53,545 --> 00:41:56,178
He was just seeing
if I'd take the bait.

654
00:41:58,850 --> 00:42:00,950
And I did.

655
00:42:21,105 --> 00:42:24,039
♪ ♪

656
00:43:05,549 --> 00:43:06,649
Oh.

657
00:43:06,717 --> 00:43:08,050
Hello, Dr. Clark.

658
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:09,764
I'm sorry... visitors
aren't permitted in here.

659
00:43:09,788 --> 00:43:11,320
Oh, I'm not...
I'm not a visitor.

660
00:43:11,389 --> 00:43:12,454
I'm Ben Matlock.

661
00:43:12,523 --> 00:43:14,490
You haven't been
returning my calls, Doctor.

662
00:43:14,558 --> 00:43:16,058
Well, I can't talk to you now.

663
00:43:16,127 --> 00:43:18,205
I'm afraid you're going to
have to make an appointment.

664
00:43:18,229 --> 00:43:20,069
Well, uh... well, this
will only take a moment.

665
00:43:20,097 --> 00:43:22,665
What can you tell me
about Michael Russell?

666
00:43:23,734 --> 00:43:26,636
Michael Russell...
Never heard of him.

667
00:43:26,704 --> 00:43:28,270
Well, I have this ledger.

668
00:43:47,058 --> 00:43:49,591
What, uh... happened to him?

669
00:43:50,895 --> 00:43:52,495
At some point, he died.

670
00:43:52,563 --> 00:43:54,475
Mr. Matlock, you
can see I'm busy.

671
00:43:54,499 --> 00:43:55,499
Not too busy

672
00:43:55,533 --> 00:43:58,167
to meet with Mr. Baldwin
and Mr. Kramer

673
00:43:58,236 --> 00:44:00,136
last night. You're all

674
00:44:00,205 --> 00:44:02,472
secret partners in,
uh, Michael Russell's

675
00:44:02,540 --> 00:44:04,474
pharmaceutical
company, aren't you?

676
00:44:04,542 --> 00:44:07,443
Leave now, or I'll
call a security guard.

677
00:44:32,303 --> 00:44:33,402
Sorry to interrupt.

678
00:44:33,471 --> 00:44:36,271
I just wanted to see
if you were interested.

679
00:45:21,252 --> 00:45:24,186
♪ ♪

680
00:45:49,847 --> 00:45:52,681
♪ ♪

681
00:46:28,953 --> 00:46:32,521
<i>I think Shelby's gone
and she's not coming back.</i>

682
00:46:33,657 --> 00:46:36,125
I'm under a lot of
pressure to go home.

683
00:46:36,194 --> 00:46:38,572
Might not be a bad idea.

684
00:46:38,596 --> 00:46:39,928
So, what should I do?

685
00:46:39,997 --> 00:46:42,965
Give up? Throw
away my whole career?

686
00:46:43,033 --> 00:46:45,045
Well, a thing like
that's up to you.

687
00:46:45,069 --> 00:46:46,680
Would you like a hot dog?

